Z||000004||007DOUG||08-30-2000||11:37 AM||||Keep in mind your 84 has ribbed mouldings. If change to a later facia with rounded moulding, you may want to change all the mouldings (including side marker lights) to match.  <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Old Lar||08-30-2000||02:32 PM||||There were new front GT fascias at Carlisle.  Wayne's World wanted $375, still in the box.  Hank Venhorst had one at that time for $350.  You may find them cheaper if you check around.||||reg||10
Z||000006||DjKid||08-30-2000||02:59 PM||||I was quoted at 125-150$ a piece for em, not too bad.. I wanna add em to my  88 Coupe... but kinda dont cuz I dont want it to look like a SE.. Bah.. I guess I'll look around see what kind of fascia's look good <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>DjKid - 88 Coupe<BR>'Blue Knight"||||reg||1
Z||000007||HugGRRRFiero||08-30-2000||03:20 PM||||Keep your eyes out for 84 Indy, or 85 GT facias.  They are the ones with the correct grooved side trim to match your existing trim.  <P>  You will need some brackets, energy absorber, and inner wheelhouse inner panels from a GT.  To save some money, the coupe front energy absorber can be modified to work with the GT nose, and you could make filler panels for the coupe style wheelhouses from some spare junk inner wheelhouse plastic if you can't find GT ones.<P>Used front & rear bumpers can run anywhere from $150 to $350 each depending on condition and if the mounting brackets are included.<P>Paint probably will cost around $200 for both the front and rear cover depending on shop labor costs.  If your paint is showing age then you might want to see how much the shop could paint your whole car or blend the paint into the fenders and quarters to get a better match.<P>If you bolt them on yourself and find pretty good deals, your looking at probably around $500 for the bumper covers and paint.<P>Post a "Wanted: 84-85 GT style bumpers" in the mall and you'll probably get some hits.  Looks like your already getting hits here.  GT will work, but I believe GM called the front cover the "Aero" fascia...  Sorry<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||08-30-2000||10:02 PM||||I've got front and rear aero fascias from an 86 SE, ribbed moulding. All crush inserts etc included. front fair, rear perfect (black). $150 each, but you must be able to pick them up in eastern PA, I will not ship them! Have you ever tried to file a damage claim with UPS?! Pics available if interested.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||7
Z||000009||Homicidal||08-31-2000||01:25 PM||||I don't want Aero fascias, I want the ones off the GT's like HugGRR's Fiero.  ||||reg||1
